name: Default
loadPath: Local
packing: PackTogether
bundleNaming: FilenameHash

# Everything in this group is a gameplay definition, said once rather than in every sidecar.
# Vixen.Gameplay.Content's DefinitionContent.LoadAsync looks for exactly this label at boot, and a
# build without it succeeds and hands a running shard an empty catalog — which is what a shard with
# no loot, no quests and no camps looks like from the outside.
#
# ⚠ It is not enough on its own, and running the shard against a real build of this tree is what
# showed why. A group is inherited from the nearest ancestor *folder*, and Assets/Maps holds both a
# zone's MapDefinition and the .vxscene it is a chart of — so this label sweeps the thirteen scenes
# in with the definitions and the realm refuses to start with thirteen "labelled a definition and did
# not read as one" problems. Splitting them needs `addressable.group` on each scene's sidecar and a
# second .vxgroup for them to name, which is part of the address decision this sample still owes:
# see Samples/14-Mmo/README.md § The content build.
labels:
  - definitions
